.TH YGGR 1 "August 2026" "yggr 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yggr \- standalone editor test bed for kat800
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yggr
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Yggr
is kat800's built\-in editor pulled out into its own GTK4 window, so editor
features can be prototyped against a real buffer without rebuilding and driving
a whole terminal emulator to reach one pane. Language Server Protocol
integration is the current example: diagnostics, hover, completion and
whole\-document formatting are proven here first and then folded back into
kat800.
.PP
It is a proving ground, not a general\-purpose editor. The surface is
deliberately small and stays small.
.PP
With no
.IR FILE ,
Yggr opens an empty buffer. Language detection, and therefore which server is
started, follows GtkSourceView's language guessing for the opened file.
.SH LANGUAGE SERVERS
Servers are never spawned directly. One is resolved in three steps, first match
winning:
.IP 1. 4
.B $YGGR_LSP_CMD
\(em an explicit command, intended for testing.
.IP 2. 4
A bundled registry
.RI ( lsp-servers.conf ),
which is how the Flatpak build supplies servers inside its sandbox.
.IP 3. 4
The
.B Foundry
CLI, as
.BR "foundry lsp run " \fILANGUAGE\fR .
.PP
This package bundles no servers: install
.B foundry
or set
.BR $YGGR_LSP_CMD .
The Flatpak build is the batteries\-included one, carrying OLS and a runnable
Odin toolchain.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YGGR_LSP_CMD
Command to run as the language server, bypassing the registry and Foundry.
.TP
.B YGGR_FOUNDRY_BIN
Path to the
.B foundry
binary when it is not on
.BR $PATH .
.TP
.B YGGR_LSP_TRACE
Set to
.B 1
to trace LSP traffic on stderr.
.TP
.B YGGR_LOCALEDIR
Message\-catalogue directory, searched before the installed location \(em set it
to run a build without installing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/yggr/lsp-servers.conf
Server registry consulted before Foundry.
.TP
.I /usr/share/gtksourceview-5/language-specs/odin.lang
Odin syntax definition; GtkSourceView ships no upstream Odin spec.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kat800 (1)
.PP
Full documentation, including the Flatpak packaging spec, is in
.I /usr/share/doc/yggr
and at https://github.com/Hyperquader-Coders/yggr
